Z||000010||fropuff||12-03-2000||06:48 PM||||I found another drag strip.  It's at Moorhead; the Brainerd one didn't look that nice.  Anyway:  it accepts DAILY DRIVERS, $40 on Sunday, $25 on Saturday.  For the Minneapolis members, go west on 94 until you reach Moorhead.  It's around there somewhere.  The web site is:  <A HREF="http://www.interstatedragways.com/Home1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.interstatedragways.com/Home1.htm</A>   I'm going to ask them some questions; anything in particular you want me to ask?  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.<p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||DrRodey||12-03-2000||11:13 PM||||Sorry, i was away for most of the weekend though.  I'm glad i got your attention though and thanks for the interest.  it's good to see that there are so many of us on here from the great white north.  <P>Ok on with Business.  The Drag strip stuff is a great idea for those who want to partake in it.  What else will we have though.  If we get this big enough we might even be able to turn it into a major yearly event, after all the next closest that i know of is the Dells Run in WI.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||12-03-2000||11:50 PM||||Fro,<BR>Ask about group discounts if they have any, and if they do a safety/tech inspection(I'm sure they do) and what they look for.  Great job on finding it!<P>Another fun trip would be to Road America, in Elkhart Lake, WI.  About a 5 hour drive, but it's a 4 mile track with a few flat-out high speed sections.<P>I'll be more than willing to help out with any planning/organizing for anything!<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||fropuff||12-04-2000||05:18 PM||||Okay, I just sent them another e-mail with some more questions.  It was an AOL address, so it will probably be answered quicker than the other one.  I asked: the safety inspection (they DO have one)-what they look for, the group discount, the price, if I can use nitrous (hopefully I'll have it by then  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">), and if 16-year-olds can race.  I hope so; then me and blayde8 can race as well.  I told them we will have valid driver's licenses, so we need to get them.  Hopefully they will answer quickly.  I will tell you what they said.  We don't have to go to a strip, we can go to an oval track instead.  It doesn't matter to me.  We should at least have a MN get-together. (anyone else can come too-WI, ND, SD, IA, etc.)  I'll get back to you.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tina||12-05-2000||01:25 AM||||Hmmm, the possibilties<BR>What else can we do you ask, DrR....?<BR>Well you can bring the hamburgers,I will the<BR>b....     Just kidding!<BR>Well for starters hopefully we would have a whole bunch of fiero's to look at, and some to watch on the strip and on the track<BR>Definitly need a 1/4 mile strip,did I mention that already.<BR>I'am sure some of the local After market Co.<BR>wouldn't mind selling their stuff their.<BR>Anybody know of some Body-shop's they can recommend, and invite to fish for business.<BR>Maybe Fiero-Dave from Wi and some of it's stuff and cars for sale would come if we asked him nicely.<BR>Portable Dyno, for people who want to get some stats the easy way.<BR>If you guys want it big, we can make it big.<P>Well just some idea's of the top of my head.<P>Uhh, how about a Wheels-Display for Aftermarket wheels that actually fit a Fiero.<P>Big enough?<BR>Later, Tina<P><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 12-05-2000).]||||reg||3
