Z||000016||fropuff||12-06-2000||06:41 PM||||Okay, I got a few answers.  The tech guy is gone until the weekend, but his wife answered a few of them.  I will tell you what she said:<BR>-As far as blayde8 and myself goes, our parents have to sign a waiver for us to race.  <BR>-$25 on Saturday is for the entire day.  She said Saturday is usually a test and tune day.<BR>-She said it'll be fine if we came.  Last year, they had the ricers.  She actually called them ricers!  Quote: "Last year we had the rice burners little cars".  Smart lady.<BR>-She didn't know the answer about nitrous, but it doesn't matter to me if I can use it or not.  It's not fair to waste a Fiero anyway.  I might not have it by then either.<BR>-She said July or August should be fine; the schedule would be finalized in January.  <P>I will reply with any more information, or if there are any changes.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000017||blayde8||12-07-2000||04:40 PM||||Thanks for the information Fropuff.  That sounds great.  I'm sure your 2.8 w/nitrous will smoke my little duke any day.  You just gotta be carefull with that nitrous, don't do anything stupid that will ruin your engine.||||reg||1
Z||000018||fropuff||12-09-2000||05:52 PM||||I got the reply.  I will tell you what it said:  <BR>"Thank for your e-mail !  I'll try to cover all of this as best I can,  we'll start with driver credentials..   Yes, regardless of age you will all need valid state drivers liscences   the 16 year olds would need to have both parents with them  to fill out and sign a minor waiver form.  The V8 car depending on if it were to go 9.99 et in the quarter mile would need a NHRA physical and liscening form filled out before you came up.      <BR>We have those forms available if nessecary.     	The basics for equip. on the car would be as follows,  coolant overflow can of at least 16 oz,  the battery held in place with either the factory holdown or a metal strap and 2   3/8 holdown bolts,  seat belts and seat all in good condition, for anyone running 13:99 or quicker a 85 or newer sfi helmet is required.  Of course wheels, tires , brakes,and steering all in good condition.  If anyone of you has a NHRA rule book follow the rules for the e.t. that your car runs..   Or call me at  701-293-0097 ask for Tim.   The $25 dollars does cover all day saturday, and no there would be no discount for a group simply because we need that amount to cover the insurance and help.  There is also a $25 dollar to enter jackpot race on Sat. afternoon with the money going back to the top 8 cars. I guess that covers it for now hopefully we can work together and see you at the races.  Try to let us know so we can help you pick a saturday once we have our schedule set for the year."  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
